  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the sum of the measures of the six minor arcs on the circumcircle of triangle \\( \\triangle DEF \\), given that the points \\( G, D, E, H, J, \\) and \\( F \\) divide the circumcircle into these arcs.\n\nFirst, we need to understand the properties of the triangle and the circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\). The angles of \\( \\triangle ABC \\) are \\( \\angle BAC = 84^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle ABC = 60^\\circ \\), and \\( \\angle ACB = 36^\\circ \\). The midpoints \\( D, E, \\) and \\( F \\) divide the sides into equal segments, and thus the triangle \\( \\triangle DEF \\) is the medial triangle of \\( \\triangle ABC \\).\n\nThe angles of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) can be determined using the properties of the medial triangle. Since \\( D, E, \\) and \\( F \\) are midpoints, the angles of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) are half the angles of \\( \\triangle ABC \\). Therefore, the angles of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) are \\( \\angle DEF = 24^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle EFD = 30^\\circ \\), and \\( \\angle FDE = 126^\\circ \\).\n\nNext, we need to find the measures of the minor arcs on the circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\). The angles subtended by these arcs at the center of the circumcircle are twice the angles at the vertices of \\( \\triangle DEF \\).\n\nThe measure of arc \\( \\widehat{DE} \\) is twice the angle \\( \\angle FDE \\), so \\( \\widehat{DE} = 2 \\cdot 126^\\circ = 252^\\circ \\).\n\nThe measure of arc \\( \\widehat{HJ} \\) is twice the angle \\( \\angle EFD \\), so \\( \\widehat{HJ} = 2 \\cdot 30^\\circ = 60^\\circ \\).\n\nThe measure of arc \\( \\widehat{FG} \\) is twice the angle \\( \\angle DEF \\), so \\( \\widehat{FG} = 2 \\cdot 24^\\circ = 48^\\circ \\).\n\nNow, we can find the sum \\( \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 252^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 60^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 48^\\circ = 252^\\circ + 120^\\circ + 144^\\circ = 516^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{516}\n\\]",
